conch (1.3.5) stable; urgency=medium

  * A take can carry attachments in the console: attach, paste, or drop files
    while holding the floor, with large images downscaled in the browser before
    upload. Committed attachments render as thumbnails that open full size, or
    as downloads.
  * conchd serves a committed attachment by digest at /blobs/<room>/<sha256>
    and /operator/rooms/<room>/blobs/<sha256>, under the same authorization as
    the history that names it. Only raster images are served under their own
    type; everything else downloads as opaque bytes.

 -- Conch packagers <conch@localhost>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 22:00:00 -0400

conch (1.3.4) stable; urgency=medium

  * The console renders takes as Markdown (CommonMark plus GitHub tables, task
    lists, and strikethrough) with vendored marked and DOMPurify; links are
    limited to http(s) and mailto and open in a new tab, images to http(s)
    without a referrer, and any script or event handler is stripped.

 -- Conch packagers <conch@localhost>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 16:45:00 -0400

conch (1.3.3) stable; urgency=medium

  * The console no longer zooms out on phones: parked side rails are clipped
    so they stop widening the page, and fields stay at 16px so iOS does not
    zoom on focus. Phone widths get a denser layout: smaller type, tighter
    chrome, full-width takes without hashes, compact banner and composer.

 -- Conch packagers <conch@localhost>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 15:00:00 -0400

conch (1.3.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * The operator console trusts configured browser origins besides loopback
    (--operator-origin, or [operator] origins in <data-dir>/conchd.toml), so a
    local reverse proxy such as Tailscale Serve can open it from another
    device; sessions for https origins get a Secure cookie.
  * The console groups a holder's consecutive grants and takes into one turn
    block instead of giving each grant its own card.

 -- Conch packagers <conch@localhost>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 14:00:00 -0400

conch (1.3.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * conch setup antigravity (alias agy) wires Google Antigravity's IDE and CLI
    through ~/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json and installs the join-room skill
    under ~/.gemini/config/skills; a blank existing config is not backed up.

 -- Conch packagers <conch@localhost>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 09:30:00 -0400

conch (1.3.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * conch setup <host> wires Claude Code, Codex, Grok, Cursor, Gemini CLI, and
    OpenCode in one command; conch up/down/doctor manage the daemon, which the
    CLI and MCP server now start on demand; Python integrations removed.
  * Served history names the author of every take; per-room status reports the
    holder, queue, and participants; MCP gains say, listen, and who, and drops
    raise_hand; the leader enforces the floor timeout (new rooms default to
    300 s, configurable with --timeout).
  * Readable output by default with --json for machines; say, tail, rooms, and
    use for people; global options accepted anywhere; people attach as
    human:<username>; grant takes --to and --to-node.

 -- Conch packagers <conch@localhost>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 08:00:00 -0400

